{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1790836943","published":"2026-10-01T06:42:36Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:15.378108885Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-11940","CVE-2026-82049"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-11940, CVE-2026-82049","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: change of permissions and modification time of a file\n     outside the destination via a tar hard link to a symlink\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-82049.patch: resolve the target of a hard\n       link member with os.path.realpath() in TarFile.makelink() in\n       Lib/tarfile.py, so the extracted hard link points to the file itself\n       instead of duplicating a symlink whose relative target escapes the\n       destination directory; make both link calls inside the upstream\n       AttributeError/NotImplementedError/OSError envelope, so a link\n       refused by the system (e.g. link(2) on a directory) falls back to\n       extracting the linked member instead of aborting the extraction\n     - CVE-2026-82049\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: tar extraction filter bypass via a hard link to a\n     symlink stored at a deeper name\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-11940.patch: pass the member that a hard link\n       falls back to extracting through the extraction filter, under its own\n       name and under the link's name, in TarFile.makelink_with_filter() in\n       Lib/tarfile.py, and raise LinkFallbackError when the filter rejects\n       it, so a symlink validated at its deeper archived name can no longer\n       be recreated at the link's shallower path outside the destination;\n       skip that member when the filter returns None for it under the\n       link's name instead of extracting it anyway\n     - CVE-2026-11940\n   * debian/rules: run test_tarfile verbosely in the check target, so the\n     result of each tarfile test appears in the build log","affected":[{"package":{"name":"idle-python2.7","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/idle-python2.7?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type"